2026-05-27 17:17:20,849 [INFO] ATHENA  : Cross-Entropy Loss vs Focal Loss

Cross-Entropy Loss (CE): It measures the probability of the correct label being predicted based on the input labels. Cross-Entropy Loss is used for regression problems where the output variable takes values between -1 and +1. CE loss is calculated as follows:

   CE = -log(y_hat) * y_true

where y_hat is the estimated value of the output variable, and y_true is the true value of the output variable.

